      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q10-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$5x^2-4x-10=0$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{2\\pm3\\sqrt6}{5}$.\n\nUse the quadratic formula and simplify $\\sqrt{216}=6\\sqrt6$.",
          "worked": "Use the quadratic formula with $a=5$, $b=-4$ and $c=-10$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-4)\\pm\\sqrt{(-4)^2-4(5)(-10)}}{2(5)}\\\\x&=\\frac{4\\pm\\sqrt{216}}{10}\\\\x&=\\frac{4\\pm6\\sqrt6}{10}\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm3\\sqrt6}{5}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q11-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$2x^2+9x+4=0$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-4$ or $x=-\\dfrac12$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2x+1)(x+4)&=0\\\\2x+1&=0\\text{ or }x+4=0\\\\x&=-\\frac12\\text{ or }x=-4\\end{align*}$$",
