        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q15-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$$2x^2-6x+1=0$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{3\\pm\\sqrt7}{2}$.\n\nUse the quadratic formula with discriminant $28$.",
          "worked": "Use the quadratic formula with $a=2$, $b=-6$ and $c=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{-(-6)\\pm\\sqrt{(-6)^2-4(2)(1)}}{2(2)}\\\\x&=\\frac{6\\pm\\sqrt{28}}{4}\\\\x&=\\frac{6\\pm2\\sqrt7}{4}\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt7}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q16-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$$x^2-8x+14=0$$",
